
A zero-arg computed function whose body calls an async native is lowered by the
NoAsyncReactive pass: the reactive read site becomes a synchronous state-field
access, and an async kicker fires at startup to fill that field.

greeting is lowered in place into three pieces -- the settled-state field
__async_greeting holding the zero value "", the kicker $compute_greeting that
awaits the fetchHello call and resolves it, and greeting itself, now a
synchronous read of the field. The kicker is called at startup, so the
initial value is fetched.

The prop that calls greeting() is not hoisted: named computeds are lowered
before inline async expressions are, so by then the call is a plain read. The
other order wrapped it in a __hoist_0 marked async that awaited a function no
longer async -- `await` outside an `async` function -- which was hidden while
the optimizer inlined greeting into the prop. It stopped doing that once a
call to an undeclared native made greeting read-only rather than pure.

deny out/none/html/index.html `__hoist_` -- a call to a named computed is not hoisted a second time
-- app.sngl --
import . "sngl:ui"
import api "js:./api"

output {
    none {
        html
    }
}

func greeting() => api.fetchHello("world")

component main node {
    text(value=greeting())
}

window {
    main
}
-- api/index.ts --
export async function fetchHello(name: string): Promise<string> { return "hi " + name; }
